# Line-ending and diff policy for the whole repository.
#
# The repository stores text with LF. Before this file existed, 55 tracked files
# were committed with CRLF (most of internal/api/web/, plus LICENSE and the two
# files under LICENSES/), and an editor or script that wrote LF back over one of
# them produced a whole-file diff that buried the real change. `eol=lf` pins the
# answer for everyone, on every platform, so that cannot happen again.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text by content, which is why no explicit
# binary list is needed beyond the image types below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images and other binary payloads must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Vendored licence texts are kept verbatim in content but normalised to LF like
# everything else; they are read as text, not executed.
LICENSE text eol=lf
LICENSES/*.txt text eol=lf

# Lockfiles and generated data are still text, but they are never hand-edited,
# so keep them out of diffs reviewers have to read.
internal/api/web/package-lock.json -diff
internal/api/web/public/world-110m.geo.json -diff
